.env file → docker-compose.yml → Spring Boot Container → application.properties


## Simplified Flow:
```
┌─────────────┐
│   .env      │  ← Define values ONCE here
│             │
│ AWS_BUCKET  │
│ AWS_KEY     │
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       ↓
┌──────────────────────┐
│ docker-compose.yml   │  ← Reference .env variables
│                      │
│ environment:         │
│   - AWS_BUCKET=${..} │
└──────┬───────────────┘
       │
       ↓
┌──────────────────────┐
│ Container            │  ← Environment variables available
│                      │
│ AWS_BUCKET_NAME=...  │
└──────┬───────────────┘
       │
       ↓
┌──────────────────────┐
│ application.props    │  ← Read from environment
│                      │
│ aws.bucket.name=     │
│   ${AWS_BUCKET_NAME} │
└──────────────────────┘


# Test if container can reach internet
docker exec music-web-application ping -c 3 google.com

# Test S3 endpoint resolution
docker exec music-web-application nslookup s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com

# Test if container can reach S3
docker exec music-web-application curl -I https://s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com


